  "phases": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "title": "Crescent deployment",
      "time": "morning, 2 August 216 BCE",
      "durationSec": 8,
      "narration": "The Romans, facing south with the Aufidus at their right, mass their infantry deeper than usual to punch through the centre. Hannibal bows his Gallic and Iberian infantry forward in a crescent, holding the best African troops back at the wing tips and the cavalry beside the river and on the open flank.",
      "orders": [
        {
          "unit": "car-gauls",
          "action": "hold"
        },
        {
          "unit": "rom-centre",
          "action": "hold"
        }
      ],
      "outcomes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "title": "Skirmishers and the cavalry clash at the river",
      "time": "morning",
      "durationSec": 10,
      "narration": "Light troops skirmish in front of the lines without result. Then Hasdrubal's Iberian and Gallic horse crash into the Roman citizen cavalry, which is squeezed between the river and its own infantry. Polybius says both sides fought on foot at close quarters; the Roman right wing cavalry is destroyed.",
